S166 LRC14 COCYCLE OBSTRUCTION ATLAS
status: proof-interface atlas / not an LRC14 proof
namespace: HYP-2994 / T1077
upstream signal: HYP-2992=Haar tile atlas, HYP-2993=zipper pattern atlas; this pass is the cochain/cocycle lift

COCHAIN LEDGER
C0: packet labels; endpoint-owner potentials; safe-section choices; Fejer rational centers; exact-period residues; state-lift route names
C1: certificate handoff arrows; endpoint owner transfers; smoothing/kernel gauges; Ramanujan phase shifts; source-spectrum pullbacks; local section restrictions
C2: fixed-margin Haar zeta squares; Haar tile curls; tope/cocircuit boundary curls; color-resonance squares; boundary moment curls; octahedral/K33 state-lift faces
H2: unpaired mixed Haar mode; no-hidden-kernel survivor; Johnson-harmonic F7 sector; THM-572 state-lift obstruction

OBSTRUCTION FACE DICTIONARY
- fixed_margin_square: closed local 2-cocycle; discharge=retain zeta or pair by color-compatible discrepancy; anchor=HYP-2991
- haar_fejer_dual_square: primal/dual coboundary check; discharge=match typed Haar packet to interval Fejer atom bank; anchor=HYP-2993/HYP-2981
- endpoint_tope_boundary: boundary coboundary or declared stop; discharge=open tope gives witness; AP/GW cocircuit is a stop; anchor=HYP-2986
- period_smoothing_square: torsion gauge; discharge=keep exact-period labels before smoothing or Selberg quotient; anchor=HYP-2979/HYP-2985
- source_exposure_cech_face: Cech 1-cocycle; discharge=local exposure sections glue or emit UNEXPOSED_SOURCE_KERNEL; anchor=HYP-2988/HYP-2953
- octahedral_harmonic_face: harmonic residual; discharge=failed local exits must construct HYP-2908/THM-572 state lift; anchor=HYP-2887/THM-572

