COCYCLE READOUT
1. Exact coboundaries are not optional bookkeeping: they are the only safe way to forget packet potentials.
2. Closed but non-exact local squares are useful only when a dual certificate pairs them or a named residual receives them.
3. Torsion/period classes are real proof data; squarefree and gcd quotients erase live prime-power packets.
4. F7 should be defined as a preserved harmonic residual sector, not as the complement of known tests.
5. The raw scalar shadow is the negative control: it preserves the slogan but destroys nearly every obstruction coordinate.

NEXT COMPUTABLE TESTS
1. Attach zeta signatures to HYP-2963 packet rows and count independent color-compatible mixed modes.
2. Tensor Ramanujan c_q labels with Haar tile classes to catch q=25/27/36/63/84/98/168/280/4312 side channels.
3. Group Fejer interval certificates by identical cocycle signature before interval generation.
4. Build a no-hidden-kernel Cech check: every exposure cover overlap glues or emits a named residual.
5. Define an F7 record with fields (packet fiber, mixed cocycle, harmonic sector, state-lift route, failed exits).
